  "question": {
    "text": "The maximum refractive index of a prism which permits the passage of light through it is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></math>. If the refracting angle of the prism is <math><mn>90</mn><mo>°</mo><mo>,</mo></math> then what is the value of <math><mi>n</mi></math>?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "For passing the ray from the prism,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>cosec</mi><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>cosec</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math><br /><br /><math><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">max</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mrow></math>",
    "image": null
  },
